1. Use and distribution
-----------------------

CyberPak may be used, copied, modified and distributed free of charge, as a
program and as source code, as long as all of the following conditions are
met:

a) Not commercial. Neither the program, nor parts of it, nor any work derived
   from it may be sold, rented or passed on for payment, and none of it may be
   bundled with a product that is sold. Only the plain cost of the medium and
   of shipping may be recovered. Inclusion in freely available collections,
   for example Aminet, is explicitly allowed.

b) All copyright, origin and license notices are preserved: this file and the
   notices in the header comments of the source files.

c) Modified versions are marked as modified and carry the same conditions.


2. No warranty
--------------

CyberPak is provided as it is, without any warranty. There is no promise that
it is fit for any purpose or that it works free of defects. The copyright
holder is not liable for damage arising from its use, including loss of data
or damage to hardware.


3. Origin — why these conditions
--------------------------------

CyberPak is a reimplementation of CyberAVI for 68k Amigas and stands in its
debt. The non-commercial condition under 1a) is not a whim; it follows from
that origin.

* CyberAVI is Copyright (c) 1996–1997 Thore Böckelmann and is freeware. Parts
  are ported from its source: the Cinepak decoder from
  `decoder/txt/DecodeCVID.c` (the building of the codebooks, the block loop,
  the handling of the strips) as well as the EClock time base and the
  drift-free audio clock from `CyberAVISync.mod`. The header comments of the
  files concerned name each place individually.

  CyberAVI itself is not part of this release. Under the terms of its author it
  may only be distributed complete and unmodified in its original archive.

* The documentation of CyberAVI reproduces the license notice of XAnim, to
  which decoder knowledge can be traced back. It is therefore preserved here:

      xanim.c

      Copyright (C) 1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997 by Mark Podlipec.
      All rights reserved.

      This software may be freely copied, modified and redistributed without
      fee for non-commerical purposes provided that this copyright notice is
      preserved intact on all copies and modified copies.

      There is no warranty or other guarantee of fitness of this software.
      It is provided solely "as is". The author(s) disclaim(s) all
      responsibility and liability with respect to this software's usage
      or its effect upon hardware or computer systems.

  The "non-commercial" condition there is the reason for 1a).

* Chunky-to-planar: `src/asm/c2p1x1_*.s` and `src/asm/c2p_kalms_040.s` come
  from Mikael Kalms (mikael@kalms.org, github.com/Kalmalyzer/kalms-c2p) and
  have been released into the public domain by their author. The changes
  against the original are stated in the header comment of each file.

* Not included and not affected by this license: the Amiga NDK headers, the
  cross compiler, Kickstart ROMs and the test material (film excerpts).
